COMPLIANT — graded against `rules/rule-authoring.md` (and `trust-posture.md` MUST-8 for the Wiring
shape, `hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-2 for hook-layer severity). The meta-rule set is honoured
throughout; there is nothing to report.

Both clause headings announce obligations and their bodies hold them. Clause 1 says deregistering a
consumer whose queue still holds messages is BLOCKED and fixes the ordering of the commit; clause 2
says the consumer-side counter is BLOCKED as the verifying instrument. Neither body hands back the
case its heading forbids, and neither softens the modal into a preference.

The two arms of each worked block differ in SUBSTANCE, so each contract is learnable from its block
alone: clause 1 contrasts stop-accepting-then-wait-for-zero-then-delete against delete-first-and-let
-dead-lettering-absorb-the-tail; clause 2 contrasts polling the broker's depth endpoint against
reading the consumer's own processed/received counters. The prohibited construction is shown in each
case, not gestured at.

The BLOCKED corpus holds five first-person sentences a session would really emit at the moment of
the excuse — "The queue looked empty when I checked this morning", "I'll deregister now and drain
the dead-letter queue afterwards" — rather than a taxonomy of error types.

Every justification line is one or two sentences and states a MECHANISM: a deleted subscription
stops the broker routing, so resident messages are unreachable and expire at TTL; a consumer counter
reports what that PROCESS received, so a message delivered to a sibling replica that crashed is
absent from the counter and present in the queue; a rollback restores processes but not a deleted
subscription.

The Wiring block carries the canonical eight fields in order, ending with the violation scope.
Severity is `advisory` at the hook layer and `halt-and-report` at gate-review, which is the direction
`hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-2 requires. The Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — a patch
deleting a `subscriptions:` entry while no command in the session's tool history calls the depth
endpoint for that queue name — which are parsed facts over one diff and one command log, so it books
enforcement that can actually arrive.

Origin carries a dated incident with its mechanism (the dashboard reported what two surviving
replicas received, not the depth of the four queues being removed) and its measured blast radius
(11,400 messages, four queues, a 24-hour TTL), and closes on what that implies about the rule's FORM:
the instrument was the failure, which is why the rule is two clauses rather than one.

SHARED FURNITURE — NOT SCOREABLE. The YAML frontmatter, the title, the four `## ` headings, the
MUST NOT bullet text, the six non-severity Wiring fields, and the first Origin paragraph are shared
byte-for-byte with a sibling pole. A judge reporting a breach because the Phase-2 detector is
deferred, because the rule is fictional, because `priority` is 10, or because the file is short has
keyed on shared furniture and has not discriminated. Heading skeleton, numbered-clause count,
justification-line count and worked-block count are identical across the pair at a size ratio of
1.25, so shape answers nothing.
